  "result": "The gate never got to judge my rule or witnesses: both real runs returned **SCOPE_VIOLATION**, and the cause is outside my two files. That also means neither file has been built or checked.\n\n**Why the gate fails:** the changed files it lists are all under `.runtime/tmp/claude-154266/…`. They are the runtime's task-output files, from this session and from other sessions running at the same time. Each gate run writes a new one of these files itself, so no edit to the node's files can clear the verdict. The scope check needs to ignore `.runtime/tmp/`, or the runtime's temp directory has to move outside the worktree.\n\n**Budget:** two of my early shell calls weren't needed, and one of them invoked the gate (output thrown away), so it probably used a run. With the two real runs, about 3 of the 6 are used. I stopped there because more runs would hit the same failure.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_22_010.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a vehicle under `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject's speed is above `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n- **What it requires:**\n  - no contact with any other road user; and\n  - for any road user ahead of the subject in its lane, the centres must not come closer than `p.conflict_centre_clearance` within `p.attention_ttc_min`.\n- **One narrowing, on h2:** the record says \"no road user and no structure\", but `rel.contact` only relates two road users. The rule therefore doesn't check contact with structures. If that matters, the plan would need to claim another atom (for example `rel.occupies` against an obstruction).\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_22_010.lean`):\n- the five planned ones: `forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind`, `branch_1`;\n- one extra, `branch_2` (violated): a car in the next lane overlaps the subject's body, so contact alone decides it.\n\nAfter the last gate run I renamed one helper in the witness file (`step` → `sampleStep`) to avoid a possible name clash. Nothing else changed.\n\nThe harness re-runs the gate on its own after this session; it can only judge these files if `.runtime/tmp` is excluded from the scope check. The full run log and choices are in `task_result.md`.",
